<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Custom garage builders in Calgary are independent firms, and this site puts you in touch with them. It builds nothing, pulls no permits and holds no licence; the builder who quotes your job contracts directly with you. This page lays out what a custom garage involves, so the quotes you collect describe the same building.</p><p>Custom usually means one or more of these: a door bigger than standard for a truck or RV, walls tall enough for a hoist or lift, a third bay, a workshop with its own power, or insulation and heat so the space works in January. Each one changes the structure, the permit path or the electrical service, and each shows up as a separate line on a quote. The sections below name those lines, with the prices Calgary builders publish and the City rules that set the limits. Every figure is attributed to whoever published it, and none of them is a quote from this site.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Oversized and tall doors</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">One Calgary builder lists 18 x 7 ft and 18 x 8 ft insulated steel doors and a 9 ft ceiling as add-ons to its packages. Write down the clear opening you need instead of asking for 'oversized'.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Wall height for a lift or hoist</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The Land Use Bylaw sets 4.6 m overall and 3.0 m at the eaveline for a garage. Taller than that is a development permit application, and the City gives no guarantee of approval.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Triple bays and long layouts</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Builders advertise triples at sizes such as 30 x 24 ft and 36 x 20 ft. Over 55 m² (592 sq ft) the City wants an engineer-designed slab unless the foundation goes 1.2 m below grade.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Workshop power</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Advertised packages run from a 15 amp service to a 240V 30A or 40-amp subpanel. A new garage always needs a separate electrical permit, and only a Master Electrician can pull it for a contractor.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Insulation and heat</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Calgary builders price insulation, drywall, a gas unit heater or in-floor heat as separate add-ons. A gas heater also needs a gas permit.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Storage attics and lofts</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Calgary's bylaw allows an attic inside the single storey, reached by a removable ladder, with no windows and a 1.5 m maximum height. Rocky View County treats a second floor or mezzanine as a site-specific engineering job.</p>
      </div>
</div>
